WEBVTT

00:00:01.870 --> 00:00:03.340
<i>Shangri-la.</i>

00:00:06.690 --> 00:00:10.690
<i>A disorderly yet peaceful land where 
people and demons, science and magic</i>

00:00:10.690 --> 00:00:13.360
<i>have established coexistence.</i>

00:00:14.540 --> 00:00:18.740
<i>However, that balance has suddenly crumbled.</i>

00:00:18.740 --> 00:00:23.290
<i>Because of the negative aura that 
started to spread from the West,</i>

00:00:23.290 --> 00:00:29.050
<i>the land has turned to ruin and 
the demons have become violent.</i>

00:00:29.770 --> 00:00:33.800
<i>And so the utopia that was once
 upheld by faith and civilization</i>

00:00:33.800 --> 00:00:37.710
<i>was completely swallowed by chaos.</i>

00:00:44.390 --> 00:00:47.810
<b>Episode 1   "Squall"</b>

00:00:57.740 --> 00:00:59.520
They're coming from behind, too!
 Break through!

00:01:06.980 --> 00:01:11.800
And we were trying so hard to quietly 
follow you back to your village, too...

00:01:12.740 --> 00:01:16.790
Humans are so guarded these days.

00:01:16.790 --> 00:01:18.370
What's with that look?

00:01:18.370 --> 00:01:21.650
Who do you think you are, you damn human?

00:01:24.180 --> 00:01:27.130
You don't want to go through that, too, do ya?

00:01:27.130 --> 00:01:28.750
Why don't we make a deal?

00:01:28.750 --> 00:01:32.150
If you lead us to your village, 
we'll spare your life.

00:01:32.560 --> 00:01:33.640
It's no use!

00:01:36.470 --> 00:01:39.730
I see. Then I guess today you're both...

00:01:40.230 --> 00:01:41.740
our prey.

00:01:59.850 --> 00:02:02.380
Wh-Who the hell are you guys?!

00:02:02.840 --> 00:02:04.440
If you're going to get in our way—

00:02:04.440 --> 00:02:06.140
The ones in the way right now

00:02:06.480 --> 00:02:08.930
are you assholes blocking the damn road!

00:02:11.240 --> 00:02:12.250
Wha—

00:02:25.640 --> 00:02:27.240
Hey! Let's get the hell outta here!

00:02:35.470 --> 00:02:37.970
Who... are you?

00:04:30.500 --> 00:04:31.630
What the...

00:04:43.730 --> 00:04:45.630
Damn it. Why are you causing trouble?

00:04:46.130 --> 00:04:48.550
How could you bring 
outsiders into our village?

00:04:48.550 --> 00:04:51.090
Have you forgotten the position we're in?

00:04:51.350 --> 00:04:55.090
I didn't have a choice. 
They saved our lives.

00:04:55.410 --> 00:04:59.860
Our donkey was killed, so they even 
hauled all of our things in their car.

00:04:59.860 --> 00:05:03.930
Even so... Look at how seedy 
they look, despite being so young.

00:05:03.940 --> 00:05:06.450
I heard that there's some 
great priest heading west

00:05:06.450 --> 00:05:10.200
to defeat all of the demons of the world, but...

00:05:10.200 --> 00:05:12.740
You mean the Sanzo priest, right?

00:05:12.740 --> 00:05:15.170
The one that's on a journey 
with his followers.

00:05:14.070 --> 00:05:15.150
Ow!

00:05:15.170 --> 00:05:18.690
I heard that they're a very 
noble and graceful group.

00:05:18.690 --> 00:05:22.270
There's no telling when the 
demons will find this village!

00:05:22.270 --> 00:05:24.790
We need them to leave as soon as possible.

00:05:24.790 --> 00:05:26.190
Exactly!

00:05:31.620 --> 00:05:33.060
<i>These people...</i>

00:05:33.430 --> 00:05:35.090
<i>smell like the outside.</i>

00:05:36.560 --> 00:05:38.140
They reek of sweat.

00:05:40.730 --> 00:05:42.490
I'm terribly sorry.

00:05:42.480 --> 00:05:45.070
Not only were you kind enough 
to feed us after we barged in,

00:05:45.070 --> 00:05:46.400
but then we ended up falling asleep.

00:05:46.400 --> 00:05:50.610
It's been so long since we had anything to 
eat or drink, much less a good night's rest.

00:05:50.610 --> 00:05:51.820
It's fine.

00:05:51.820 --> 00:05:54.300
I heard that you guys saved my dad.

00:05:55.210 --> 00:05:56.510
Where did you come from?

00:05:56.510 --> 00:05:57.700
Chang'an.

00:05:58.500 --> 00:05:59.570
Chang'an?

00:05:59.850 --> 00:06:06.660
It's the biggest and most lively city 
in all of Shangri-la, far east of here.

00:06:06.660 --> 00:06:07.460
Huh...

00:06:08.500 --> 00:06:11.230
I'm surprised you made it 
this far in one piece.

00:06:12.570 --> 00:06:15.520
I totally thought I was gonna die this time.

00:06:15.520 --> 00:06:17.150
What? From starvation?

00:06:17.150 --> 00:06:19.510
I'm pretty sure you've survived a lot worse.

00:06:20.590 --> 00:06:22.490
I want to take a bath.

00:06:22.490 --> 00:06:24.720
Come now, don't be so rowdy.

00:06:24.720 --> 00:06:27.950
I don't care, but the adults 
will probably say something,

00:06:28.480 --> 00:06:30.460
so it's better to be quiet.

00:06:30.760 --> 00:06:33.440
If you're too loud, the adults hit you.

00:06:33.440 --> 00:06:35.230
See? You got us in trouble.

00:06:35.230 --> 00:06:36.900
What are you blaming me?

00:06:36.900 --> 00:06:39.830
Yes, I've noticed that this 
is a very quiet village.

00:06:40.330 --> 00:06:42.570
A hidden village, even.

00:06:43.370 --> 00:06:48.330
On our way here, we saw the 
remnants of three villages,

00:06:48.330 --> 00:06:50.730
but they had all been raided.

00:06:51.330 --> 00:06:54.100
Most of the villages around here are gone.

00:06:54.520 --> 00:06:59.030
Now that you mention it, the encounter rate 
for demons in this area's been pretty insane.

00:06:59.030 --> 00:07:02.100
Yeah, thanks to that, 
my clothes are all torn up.

00:07:03.600 --> 00:07:06.330
Remember the bridge you crossed 
to get into the village?

00:07:06.820 --> 00:07:09.610
That drawbridge is usually up,

00:07:10.070 --> 00:07:13.160
so the demons haven't managed 
to find this village yet.

00:07:14.400 --> 00:07:15.360
But...

00:07:16.320 --> 00:07:22.830
But as you can see, it's a very 
gloomy and secluded village now.

00:07:23.290 --> 00:07:29.200
We've been living in fear of them for so long
 that we barely even turn the lights on.

00:07:29.940 --> 00:07:33.840
This used to be a bright, happy 
village, despite its size.

00:07:34.700 --> 00:07:36.240
You have my condolences.

00:07:37.610 --> 00:07:42.340
We don't plan to stay long. 
We're in a hurry.

00:07:42.340 --> 00:07:48.650
I'm sorry to say this, but we'll have to ask
 you all to stay until tomorrow morning.

00:07:49.380 --> 00:07:50.860
And why's that?

00:07:51.360 --> 00:07:54.320
The demons might find the village
 unless you leave around dawn or dusk.

00:07:54.320 --> 00:07:57.860
We don't use the drawbridge 
unless we absolutely have to.

00:07:58.480 --> 00:08:01.610
Dad, they said they want to take a bath.

00:08:01.610 --> 00:08:05.620
Yes, I don't doubt that. 
I'll prepare one for you now.

00:08:05.620 --> 00:08:07.980
Then let's split up into pairs.

00:08:07.980 --> 00:08:12.730
I finally get to take a bath, so why the hell
 does it have to be with another guy?

00:08:12.730 --> 00:08:15.630
I'm going to take one alone, 
so you three go in together.

00:08:15.630 --> 00:08:16.440
Hey.

00:08:16.440 --> 00:08:18.000
So how are we going to split up?

00:08:18.000 --> 00:08:19.940
Good question. Why don't we...

00:08:19.940 --> 00:08:20.560
Listen, damn it.

00:08:20.560 --> 00:08:22.680
Ready, and... Rock and paper.

00:08:26.110 --> 00:08:27.940
This feels so good!

00:08:27.940 --> 00:08:30.560
Thank goodness this village has a well.

00:08:30.560 --> 00:08:33.950
I'm gonna have Hakkai cut my hair later, too.

00:08:33.950 --> 00:08:37.950
But man, we sure ended up in a place
 with a pretty different culture...

00:08:37.950 --> 00:08:40.930
There was so much food 
we've never eaten before!

00:08:40.930 --> 00:08:42.970
The food was all you noticed?

00:08:43.290 --> 00:08:47.800
Well, we're in the western region
 of Shangri-la now, right?

00:08:47.800 --> 00:08:50.450
How much farther is it to India?

00:08:56.420 --> 00:08:58.370
What the hell is wrong 
with you two? Shut up.

00:08:58.370 --> 00:09:00.900
We told you two that we need to keep it down.

00:09:00.900 --> 00:09:03.370
A ghost! There was a scary ghost!

00:09:03.760 --> 00:09:06.270
In that window over there! 
There was a woman...

00:09:07.540 --> 00:09:13.110
Don't the peaches taste wonderful?

00:09:13.480 --> 00:09:18.500
They're blooming beautifully, aren't they?

00:09:18.820 --> 00:09:24.710
But who could be

00:09:19.070 --> 00:09:20.490
That's Rei-neesan.

00:09:21.310 --> 00:09:25.250
She's been like that ever 
since she lost her husband,

00:09:25.070 --> 00:09:28.940
kicking around in the shadows 
of the tall peach tree?

00:09:25.250 --> 00:09:27.870
so everyone in the village 
treats her like a nuisance.

00:09:28.120 --> 00:09:29.480
How dare you wander around?!

00:09:29.480 --> 00:09:31.190
Be quiet!

00:09:30.900 --> 00:09:36.000
But the peach tree is just too tall.

00:09:31.670 --> 00:09:33.770
But Rei-neesan's husband

00:09:34.090 --> 00:09:36.430
was basically murdered 
by the people of this village.

00:09:37.370 --> 00:09:39.530
On his way back from a supply run,

00:09:39.530 --> 00:09:42.430
he was attacked by some demons, 
just like my dad was today.

00:09:42.800 --> 00:09:44.780
But he was in a bad way.

00:09:45.150 --> 00:09:49.390
He was too close to the village, and the 
demons were right by the drawbridge.

00:09:50.260 --> 00:09:53.610
The villagers heard what 
was going on outside,

00:09:54.110 --> 00:09:57.000
and they chose not to lower the bridge.

00:09:57.720 --> 00:09:59.830
So it was to protect the village.

00:09:59.830 --> 00:10:02.790
If they had lowered the bridge, 
he might've survived!

00:10:03.190 --> 00:10:06.280
The villagers sacrificed one of their own!

00:10:07.480 --> 00:10:11.910
I... hate this place.

00:10:18.150 --> 00:10:20.990
I'm sure he understands deep down

00:10:21.600 --> 00:10:25.130
that the ones he should hate are 
the demons and not the villagers.

00:10:26.650 --> 00:10:28.480
Goku, Gojyo.

00:10:30.640 --> 00:10:32.440
Put some damn clothes on.

00:10:32.440 --> 00:10:34.060
Why are they undressed?

00:10:34.060 --> 00:10:35.930
This is the problem with outsiders...

00:10:35.930 --> 00:10:36.560
Oh.

00:10:36.560 --> 00:10:37.300
My bad.

00:10:38.390 --> 00:10:40.950
Don't the peaches—

00:10:41.570 --> 00:10:43.550
I told you to stop singing!

00:10:43.550 --> 00:10:46.040
You don't need to go that far...

00:10:46.040 --> 00:10:48.980
We're all trying to stay as quiet 
as possible in order to survive!

00:10:48.980 --> 00:10:52.310
If the demons find this 
village, we're finished!

00:10:52.670 --> 00:10:58.250
I'm sorry. I pity you, 
but we're all suffering, too.

00:10:58.920 --> 00:11:03.050
Tamuro's father managed to get away 
from the demons and come back.

00:11:04.580 --> 00:11:07.420
Her husband was just unlucky.

00:11:11.680 --> 00:11:14.100
A real futon!

00:11:14.430 --> 00:11:17.230
I'm sorry that we only have this tiny room.

00:11:17.230 --> 00:11:19.170
Oh, please don't apologize.

00:11:18.630 --> 00:11:19.610
You're wide open!

00:11:19.920 --> 00:11:23.580
We're just happy to have 
a roof over our heads.

00:11:20.160 --> 00:11:21.830
The hell was that for, you bastard?!

00:11:21.830 --> 00:11:23.580
I was nice enough to hand that to you!

00:11:23.580 --> 00:11:24.760
Well, I don't want it!

00:11:24.130 --> 00:11:26.770
Oh, and I'll quiet them down immediately.

00:11:27.460 --> 00:11:31.610
All right, rest well. I'll see you at 6 AM.

00:11:32.170 --> 00:11:35.250
Thank you very much. Goodnight.

00:11:37.170 --> 00:11:39.470
Wow, this is really flashy.

00:11:39.470 --> 00:11:42.550
Yes, it has a rather exotic look.
 It's quite nice.

00:11:43.260 --> 00:11:47.850
To think that the culture is so different here,
 even though we're still in Shangri-la...

00:11:47.850 --> 00:11:48.560
Yeah.

00:11:48.840 --> 00:11:51.430
That's just how far west we've come.

00:11:51.430 --> 00:11:54.130
The effects of the negative 
aura are even stronger here.

00:11:54.130 --> 00:11:57.810
The fact that we're running into 
even more demons is proof of that.

00:11:58.130 --> 00:12:01.590
We've basically stepped into enemy territory.

00:12:01.590 --> 00:12:04.990
You're telling us to brace ourselves, right?

00:12:04.990 --> 00:12:08.110
Considering what we've been through 
lately, I think we get the point.

00:12:08.870 --> 00:12:13.720
But you know, there's all this new 
stuff around us, so isn't it exciting?

00:12:13.720 --> 00:12:15.640
It feels like we're actually on a journey.

00:12:15.640 --> 00:12:19.420
We've been traveling for two years. 
What the hell are you talking about?

00:12:19.420 --> 00:12:21.790
Must be nice being a monkey.

00:12:21.790 --> 00:12:24.170
The water in this area
 isn't agreeing with me.

00:12:24.530 --> 00:12:27.070
Yeah, you went from a water sprite
 to a diarrhea sprite, huh?

00:12:27.070 --> 00:12:28.700
I don't need your pity!

00:12:28.700 --> 00:12:31.300
My stomach is just very sensitive,
 unlike your monkey guts!

00:12:31.300 --> 00:12:34.890
All right, all right. It's time to go to bed. 
We have an early morning tomorrow.

00:12:34.890 --> 00:12:37.530
I'm leaving behind whoever doesn't wake up.

00:12:37.530 --> 00:12:40.560
Ugh, don't lie in the bed like 
it was made just for you!

00:12:40.560 --> 00:12:41.730
Who the hell do you think you are?

00:12:41.730 --> 00:12:43.410
Sanzo-sama.

00:12:43.410 --> 00:12:44.590
Wow...

00:12:45.350 --> 00:12:50.370
Don't the peaches taste wonderful?

00:12:50.970 --> 00:12:56.330
They're blooming beautifully, aren't they?

00:12:56.910 --> 00:13:02.360
But who could be

00:13:02.760 --> 00:13:05.350
kicking around...

00:13:11.300 --> 00:13:12.710
Save us!

00:13:24.180 --> 00:13:25.780
D-Demons?!

00:13:28.760 --> 00:13:31.290
Come on! Open up!

00:13:31.290 --> 00:13:32.520
What's wrong, Tamuro?

00:13:32.520 --> 00:13:34.010
Dad, there are demons!

00:13:34.010 --> 00:13:35.720
There are tons of demons in the village...

00:13:35.720 --> 00:13:36.810
What?

00:13:41.610 --> 00:13:44.120
Huh? Did this door open inwards?

00:13:47.840 --> 00:13:49.590
You're disturbing everyone's beauty rest!

00:13:50.300 --> 00:13:51.010
This way.

00:13:57.440 --> 00:13:59.370
Who the hell are these guys?

00:14:00.840 --> 00:14:03.730
You woke us up two hours early.

00:14:04.300 --> 00:14:07.360
You'd better be prepared, you damn maggots.

00:14:09.990 --> 00:14:11.620
Pure white priest robes...

00:14:11.870 --> 00:14:13.660
A silver pistol...

00:14:13.660 --> 00:14:17.480
A monk priest with purple 
eyes and golden hair...

00:14:17.480 --> 00:14:18.510
And...

00:14:18.870 --> 00:14:20.630
His three

00:14:20.630 --> 00:14:23.130
demon-like followers...

00:14:23.510 --> 00:14:26.130
C-Could they actually be...

00:14:31.160 --> 00:14:33.500
the Genjo Sanzo party?!

00:14:34.720 --> 00:14:36.150
They came from the east...

00:14:36.620 --> 00:14:38.130
It's said that wherever they go,

00:14:38.630 --> 00:14:42.650
they create whole mountains of demon corpses.

00:14:43.070 --> 00:14:46.440
They're a heartless gang of wanted men.

00:14:49.970 --> 00:14:51.410
The Sanzo party?!

00:14:52.290 --> 00:14:56.910
The ones who disappeared recently 
and were rumored to be dead?

00:14:56.910 --> 00:14:59.180
Hey, don't kill us off like that.

00:14:59.160 --> 00:15:02.420
Come to think of it, there haven't 
been too many guys yelling,

00:15:02.420 --> 00:15:04.670
"Curse you, Sanzo party!" 
and attacking us lately.

00:15:04.670 --> 00:15:05.970
Perhaps...

00:15:06.660 --> 00:15:11.140
they didn't recognize us
 because we were so filthy?

00:15:11.140 --> 00:15:11.910
Seriously?

00:15:12.800 --> 00:15:17.870
Don't the peaches taste wonderful?

00:15:17.930 --> 00:15:20.090
Hold it right there, Sanzo party!

00:15:18.550 --> 00:15:21.650
They're blooming beautifully, aren't they?

00:15:20.090 --> 00:15:21.410
Throw down your weapons!

00:15:22.060 --> 00:15:23.530
Rei-oneechan!

00:15:23.940 --> 00:15:26.970
One false move and the woman dies!

00:15:24.420 --> 00:15:29.690
But who could be

00:15:26.970 --> 00:15:31.020
A great holy man wouldn't let
 an innocent woman die, would he?

00:15:31.160 --> 00:15:35.010
kicking around in the shadows 
of the tall peach tree?

00:15:31.770 --> 00:15:32.930
There it is.

00:15:32.930 --> 00:15:33.870
So annoying.

00:15:33.870 --> 00:15:36.110
How many times have we 
been in this situation?

00:15:36.110 --> 00:15:40.130
Apparently the things that villains do 
don't change much, no matter where we go.

00:15:40.130 --> 00:15:44.610
My arms won't reach...

00:15:41.420 --> 00:15:46.220
I guess I was right to keep this crazy bitch 
alive so I could have some fun with her later.

00:15:46.220 --> 00:15:47.000
Come here!

00:15:47.000 --> 00:15:48.580
Stop singing!

00:15:48.580 --> 00:15:49.860
Rei-neechan!

00:15:49.860 --> 00:15:51.220
Don't, Tamuro!

00:15:51.550 --> 00:15:52.750
Let go of me!

00:15:52.750 --> 00:15:55.670
Now you're just going to watch her die, too?!

00:15:55.670 --> 00:15:57.460
Well, I mean...

00:15:57.460 --> 00:15:59.100
You reap what you sow.

00:15:59.880 --> 00:16:04.100
It's her fault we're in this mess right now.

00:16:05.790 --> 00:16:06.920
You idiots!

00:16:06.920 --> 00:16:09.100
Why haven't any of you noticed?!

00:16:09.100 --> 00:16:10.670
Rei-neechan...

00:16:10.670 --> 00:16:13.660
The song that Rei-neechan is singing...

00:16:13.660 --> 00:16:23.200
Beneath the peaches that we all gathered, 
the one that I loved also appeared.

00:16:19.980 --> 00:16:21.130
The festival...

00:16:21.930 --> 00:16:25.000
It's the village festival song.

00:16:25.790 --> 00:16:29.250
Even though everyone here 
is living in fear of the demons,

00:16:29.250 --> 00:16:32.840
and even though she's gone mad with grief,

00:16:33.340 --> 00:16:37.540
she's still trying to teach us children that song

00:16:38.460 --> 00:16:41.640
so it won't be forgotten...

00:16:42.600 --> 00:16:46.690
So that one day when, 
we're able to have festivals again,

00:16:46.690 --> 00:16:49.070
we'll be able to sing it together.

00:16:54.090 --> 00:16:57.670
We might have been wrong.

00:16:59.580 --> 00:17:02.340
We were so focused on just surviving...

00:17:03.420 --> 00:17:10.910
But what happiness is there in a village 
where children can't play, laugh or sing?

00:17:13.050 --> 00:17:19.520
This has nothing to do with us, but 
I owe you one for a night's rest and a meal.

00:17:19.520 --> 00:17:21.730
Tell me what you want me to do.

00:17:24.760 --> 00:17:25.960
Dear...

00:17:26.890 --> 00:17:28.350
Save her...

00:17:28.540 --> 00:17:30.600
Please save her!

00:17:36.120 --> 00:17:38.850
It seems that even in a different land

00:17:38.850 --> 00:17:40.330
with a different culture,

00:17:40.860 --> 00:17:44.880
the heart of things isn't too 
different from anywhere else.

00:17:45.900 --> 00:17:48.360
Well, when you put it that way...

00:17:49.330 --> 00:17:52.940
We don't really change, 
no matter where we go, either.

00:17:56.520 --> 00:17:58.120
Hey, we've got a problem!

00:17:58.120 --> 00:18:01.140
The two other demons from earlier 
escaped toward the bridge!

00:18:01.140 --> 00:18:02.500
What?

00:18:02.510 --> 00:18:04.520
They know where the village is now.

00:18:04.520 --> 00:18:07.270
If they get out and bring 
other demons back with them...

00:18:07.280 --> 00:18:09.850
We have to do something before that happens!

00:18:10.880 --> 00:18:11.930
Hakuryu!

00:18:15.600 --> 00:18:18.390
Well, take care. The food was great!

00:18:18.390 --> 00:18:18.730
Huh?

00:18:19.290 --> 00:18:22.270
We'll excuse ourselves now.

00:18:22.540 --> 00:18:25.240
We'll squash the rats 
that got away on our way out

00:18:25.240 --> 00:18:26.910
while we're at it.

00:18:34.240 --> 00:18:37.240
Who in the world were they?

00:18:37.240 --> 00:18:39.240
They almost seemed like...

00:18:41.410 --> 00:18:43.280
a squall.

00:18:45.520 --> 00:18:47.030
You've gotta be shitting me!

00:18:47.380 --> 00:18:50.890
There's no way we could win 
against those monsters...

00:18:54.530 --> 00:18:55.100
Shit!

00:18:56.180 --> 00:18:57.840
Go! Cross now!

00:18:59.930 --> 00:19:02.060
Now they won't be able to catch up with us!

00:19:02.920 --> 00:19:04.200
Good riddance!

00:19:06.200 --> 00:19:07.710
Here we go!

00:19:10.540 --> 00:19:10.980
Huh?

00:19:10.980 --> 00:19:11.790
Wait...

00:19:17.660 --> 00:19:22.020
Don't the peaches taste wonderful?

00:19:22.020 --> 00:19:26.290
They're blooming... right good and stuff, yeah?

00:19:26.290 --> 00:19:30.170
But who could be...

00:19:29.220 --> 00:19:30.260
Shut up.

00:19:30.260 --> 00:19:32.890
I guess that song got stuck in our heads.

00:19:30.480 --> 00:19:33.730
But the peach tree is just too tall

00:19:33.230 --> 00:19:35.440
I told you to shut up!

00:19:33.980 --> 00:19:35.440
My arms won't reach...

00:19:35.440 --> 00:19:36.190
Ow!

00:19:36.590 --> 00:19:38.680
What's the harm in singing?!

00:19:38.680 --> 00:19:42.900
This never changes. It's the same 
damn pattern over and over again.

00:19:44.930 --> 00:19:48.170
If we keep up with a certain 
pattern over and over again,

00:19:48.170 --> 00:19:49.960
it becomes our own style.

00:19:53.920 --> 00:19:56.550
So the sun rises in the east.

00:19:57.550 --> 00:20:00.540
It's just as you predicted, Talche.

00:20:01.240 --> 00:20:02.820
The stars are unmistakable.

00:20:07.630 --> 00:20:11.550
The orbit of the sun is 
eternally unchanging.

00:20:11.980 --> 00:20:14.310
It rises in the east,

00:20:15.160 --> 00:20:17.150
travels westward and then sinks

00:20:18.420 --> 00:20:19.640
into the earth.

00:20:20.660 --> 00:20:24.370
The sun will fall and the land will 
be swallowed by the darkness.

00:20:26.720 --> 00:20:28.780
Is that another one of your prophecies?

00:20:30.230 --> 00:20:31.080
Nay.

00:20:31.920 --> 00:20:33.200
It is providence.

00:22:04.970 --> 00:22:09.970
<b>Episode 2
 "Cloud Mirror"</b>

00:22:05.660 --> 00:22:08.090
Episode 2, "Cloud Mirror."

00:22:08.090 --> 00:22:09.980
Watch without fail.

00:22:09.970 --> 00:22:12.970
<b>Ura Sai</b>

00:22:09.970 --> 00:22:12.970
<b>Lettering: Seki Toshihiko</b>

00:22:09.980 --> 00:22:12.980
Ready, and... Ura Sai!

00:22:12.970 --> 00:22:14.980
<b>Tanabata Festival</b>

00:22:16.950 --> 00:22:18.950
The Star Festival, huh?

00:22:18.950 --> 00:22:23.110
You sort of lose track of the 
days when you're traveling.

00:22:23.110 --> 00:22:25.810
It's important to remember 
these yearly events.

00:22:25.820 --> 00:22:31.870
I wanna eat all the meat buns

00:22:26.080 --> 00:22:29.400
"I wanna eat all the meat buns"?
That's definitely the monkey.

00:22:29.400 --> 00:22:30.720
Is everything about food to you?

00:22:30.720 --> 00:22:31.860
Shut up! Leave me alone!

00:22:32.130 --> 00:22:36.160
And I see that you wrote "debauchery," 
Gojyo. You're the same as ever.

00:22:36.160 --> 00:22:38.010
Shut up. That's every man's dream.

00:22:38.010 --> 00:22:39.370
Talk about a cheap-ass dream.

00:22:39.380 --> 00:22:41.750
<b>I wanna give a pretty lady a ride</b>

00:22:39.710 --> 00:22:41.750
Huh? Gojyo, did you write two?

00:22:42.140 --> 00:22:43.260
I didn't write that.

00:22:43.260 --> 00:22:45.650
Who the hell else would 
write something like that?

00:22:45.650 --> 00:22:48.000
Wait, this is...

00:22:49.130 --> 00:22:50.890
<b>Ura Sai</b>

00:22:49.130 --> 00:22:50.890
<b>Lettering: Seki Toshihiko</b>

00:22:49.400 --> 00:22:50.620
Ura Sai.

00:22:50.890 --> 00:22:52.470
I wanna eat all the meat buns

00:22:50.890 --> 00:22:54.140
<b>Debauchery</b>

00:22:52.470 --> 00:22:54.140
Peace and prosperity 
in the household.
Sound health.

00:22:54.270 --> 00:22:56.000
Huh? Where's yours, Sanzo?

00:22:57.540 --> 00:23:00.170
Wishes are meant to be granted on your own.

00:23:00.170 --> 00:23:01.390
You're so stubborn.

00:23:01.390 --> 00:23:03.520
Then I'll write one for you.

00:23:03.520 --> 00:23:05.480
"May my baldness be cured."
